86Box is a low level x86 emulator that specializes in running old
operating systems and software designed for IBM PC systems and
compatibles from 1981 through fairly recent system designs based on
the PCI bus.

Features include low level emulation of 8086-based processors up to
the Mendocino-era Celeron, a large range of customizable virtual
machines (from the IBM PC 5150 to various PS/2 models), and support
for many video adapters, sound cards, network adapters, hard disk
controllers and SCSI adapters.

The machine ROMs are provided by the separate emulators/86box-roms
package.
